          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.766,
            0.047,
            0.862,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Power Play"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.457,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "Similarly, $10^{-3} = \\frac{1}{10^{3}}, 7^{-2} = \\frac{1}{7^{2}}$ , etc."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.122,
            0.391,
            0.169
          ],
          "content": "Can we write $1 0 ^ { 3 } = \\frac { 1 } { 1 0 ^ { ^ { - 3 } } }   ?$ We can write,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.335,
            0.177,
            0.661,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{1}{10^{-3}} = \\frac{1}{1/10^{3}} = 1 \\div \\frac{1}{10^{3}} = 1 \\times 10^{3} = 10^{3}.",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.213,
            0.448,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": "Similarly, $\\nabla ^ { 2 } = { \\frac { 1 } { 7 ^ { -   2 } } }$ and $4 ^ { a } = { \\frac { 1 } { 4 ^ { - a } } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.244,
            0.395,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": "In a generalised form,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.332,
            0.27,
            0.664,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "$n ^ { -   a } = { \\frac { 1 } { n ^ { a } } }$ and $n ^ { a } = { \\frac { 1 } { n ^ { - a } } }$ , where $n \\neq 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.778,
            0.247,
            0.865,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "Math Talk"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.301,
            0.705,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": "Consider the following general forms we have identified."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.326,
            0.792,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "| $n^{a} \\times n^{b} = n^{a + b}$ | $( n ^ { a } ) ^ { b } = ( n ^ { b } ) ^ { a } = n ^ { a \\times b }$ | $n^{a} \\div n^{b} = n^{a - b}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.367,
            0.846,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": "？ We had required a and b to be counting numbers. Can a and b be any integers? Will the generalised forms still hold true?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.421,
            0.743,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "Write equivalent forms of the following. (i) 2– 4 (ii) $1 0 ^ { - 5 }$ $( = 7 ) ^ { - 2 }$ (iv) $( - 5 ) ^ { -   3 }$ (v) $1 0 ^ { - 1 0 0 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.494,
            0.758,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "? Simplify and write the answers in exponential form. (i) $2 ^ { - 4 } \\times 2 ^ { 7 }$ (ii) $3^{2} \\times 3^{-5} \\times 3^{6}$ (iii) $p ^ { 3 } \\times p ^ { - 1 0 }$ (iv) $2 ^ { 4 }   \\times \\left( - 4 \\right) ^ { - 2 }$ (v) $8 ^ { p } \\times 8 ^ { q }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.574,
            0.305,
            0.593
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Power Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.605,
            0.574,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": "Let us arrange the powers of 4 along a line."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
